JWasm: -Zj separates macro arguments by blanks as well as commas

MASM 5 takes a blank between two items of a macro call as an argument
separator, as a comma is. JWasm takes the whole text up to the next
comma as one argument.

Needed for STRUC.INC, whose structured-programming macros are called as
.IF <x EQ y> THEN, .WHILE <...> AND <...> and so on (MORE, MODE, FIND,
CHKDSK): the operands and the conjunctions are separate arguments.

Not for macro functions, the loop directives (anonymous macros) or a
macro's VARARG parameter, which keeps the rest of the line.

